+## Why
+
+Some clients send partial updates as JSON Merge Patch documents, which are simpler than JSON Patch. The toolkit has no way to apply them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add an exported `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` that applies a JSON Merge Patch and returns the merged document.
+- Purely additive; no existing export changes, so **no breaking changes** for importers.
+
+## Governing standard
+
+JSON Merge Patch, RFC 7396 §2 (the `MergePatch` algorithm) and §3 (the media type). The request cites RFC 7386, which RFC 7396 obsoletes with the same algorithm; the project config names 7396, so 7396 is cited.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-merge-patch`: applying an RFC 7396 merge patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new export. `test/merge-patch.test.ts`: new tests. No dependencies added.
+- Out of scope: generating a merge patch from two documents, a JSON Patch conversion, and parsing JSON text (inputs are already-parsed values).
